course: dictionary
lesson: 8181
title: Being respectful
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Respectful means showing respect: being polite and kind to other people, their feelings, their things and their beliefs. It also means treating places, animals and nature with care. Respectful is an adjective, and respectfully is the adverb, so you can speak respectfully.
explain: Use the words around it to work out the meaning. «Many families greet in their own way» tells you that people greet each other differently, so a respectful person accepts those differences. Check by swapping in your meaning: "a polite way of greeting" still makes sense.
explain: Respectful people do everyday things: they listen when others speak, take turns, and ask before borrowing. At a memorial, people stay respectfully quiet, which means they are silent to show they care.
explain: Notice the phrase "be respectful of". «When classmates celebrate Christmas, Diwali, Eid, Hanukkah or Lunar New Year, you are respectful of their traditions.» Being respectful of something means treating it with care, even when it is not yours.
fact: Respectful means showing respect: being polite and considerate.
fact: «Respectfully» is the adverb, and it means in a respectful way.
fact: «Respectful silence» is quiet that shows you honour people, such as at a memorial.
fact: You can be respectful without sharing someone's belief: «You do not have to share a belief to be respectful about it.»
fact: Respectful people accept others' choices, such as «others' food choices».
exercise: «Many families greet in their own way.» In this sentence, what does respectful mean for a greeting? | Loud enough for everyone to jump | *Polite and kind, showing you value the other person | Only used by older people | Quick, so it is over fast
exercise: Which word in «At a memorial, people stay respectfully quiet» is the adverb? | *respectfully | people | quiet | memorial
exercise: Ariana asks, «Do I have to share a belief to be respectful about it?» What is the answer? | Only if you are older | *No, you can respect someone's belief without sharing it | Respect only applies to animals | Yes, always
test: «When classmates celebrate Eid, you are respectful of their traditions.» What does being respectful of their traditions mean? | Making fun of them | Ignoring them completely | *Treating them with care and not mocking them | Laughing when they explain them
test: Which action is respectful? | Shouting across the classroom | Talking over a friend | Grabbing a pen without asking | *Asking before you borrow something
exam: Which action shows respect for nature? | Breaking branches off the trees | Chasing animals for fun | Dropping litter in the park | *Picking up litter and leaving the park as you found it
